WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.119 --> 00:00:02.700
(upbeat music)

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.210
- Hello, everyone and
welcome to the Sunglow

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:06.570
here Bicknell, Utah.

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:09.020
My name is Bessie Stewart, and today

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:12.193
we're going to make our famous pickle pie.

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:21.400
Pickle pie a dessert; it's
not the sweetest pie we have,

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.993
but it is the most original.

00:00:24.993 --> 00:00:27.540
It took a lot of imagination I
think to invent a dessert pie

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.050
with a pickle in it.

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:32.360
The original owner found
the recipe in a magazine.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:35.860
She didn't like the recipe at
all so she changed it around,

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:38.730
and now the pickle pie is the very best.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:41.430
Just far as I know we are the only place

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:42.793
that makes the pickle pie.

00:00:46.319 --> 00:00:48.986
(upbeat music)

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:54.290
In pickle pie you will
find sugar, butter, milk,

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:59.170
eggs, lemon extract, corn
starch, cinnamon, nutmeg,

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:01.950
and, of course, the pickles.

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:05.120
So we've got this all mixed
in really nice and smooth,

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:09.130
so now we're gonna pour it
into our unbaked pie shell

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:10.970
to put in the oven.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:14.510
Scrape the edges so
you get all the flavor.

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:18.550
This one right here is one
that we baked this morning.

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:20.663
Wow, pickle pie.

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:24.510
This is delicious.

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:26.880
Little tiny bit of cream on it.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:30.040
Just gives it that little
bit of sweet and sour

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:32.683
that you need to set off the taste buds.

00:01:34.212 --> 00:01:35.045
So, mmm.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:40.600
The customers like the
pickle pie, but I think

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.623
the biggest selling point is curiosity.

00:01:47.333 --> 00:01:49.775
- This looks like a delicious pie.

00:01:49.775 --> 00:01:52.330
- It tastes very similar to a pumpkin pie.

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:55.477
- It's got a hint of pickle to it.

00:01:55.477 --> 00:01:58.360
- But, it's not like
overpowering or anything.

00:01:58.360 --> 00:01:59.900
- Good flavor, sweet.

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:01.160
- A little sweet.

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:02.600
- It's, like, super sweet.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:06.383
- It's not really sweet.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:10.823
- I think it's gonna sell.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:15.330
- Bicknell is a very small little town.

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:17.960
We are about three hours
from Salt Lake City.

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:20.240
And you don't have to
live in a great big city

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:22.060
to have good food.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:26.710
You have to have pride and an imagination.

00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:28.720
It's more than just a pie.

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:30.660
It's your work of art.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:33.160
It's something that you have done.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:35.460
And it looks pretty and it tastes good,

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:36.810
and you can be proud of it.

00:02:38.151 --> 00:02:40.818
(upbeat music)

